### Scenario 10 - reservation expiry
### Start the stack with a 1 minute reservation:
###   RESERVATION_TTL_MINUTES=1 docker compose up -d --build
### Then: create the order, wait more than 1 minute, pay -> 400 and the order becomes EXPIRED
### (the order job runs every 30 s, the catalog job every minute, both release the stock)

@order = http://localhost:8083
@catalog = http://localhost:8081

# @name cart
POST {{order}}/carts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": 2 }

###
POST {{order}}/carts/{{cart.response.body.id}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELC-3001", "qty": 1 }

###
# @name checkout
POST {{order}}/carts/{{cart.response.body.id}}/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "shippingMethod": "STANDARD" }

### Stock is reserved
GET {{catalog}}/products/ELC-3001

### ... wait more than 1 minute ...

### Pay: refused, order EXPIRED
POST {{order}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.id}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "CARD", "cardNumber": "4111111111111111" }

###
GET {{order}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.id}}

### Stock is back
GET {{catalog}}/products/ELC-3001
